      "body": "[by Claude Code]\n\n## Motivation\n\nFixes #45392.\n\nSince #44975 re-enabled `test/registered/e2e/models/test_muse_spark_12_b300_pd.py`, `base-c-test-8-gpu-b300` fails on every `pull_request` run from a fork.\n\n- GitHub does not pass repository secrets to fork PRs, so `HF_MUSE_SPARK_TOKEN`, which comes from `secrets.HF_MUSE_SPARK_TOKEN` in `_pr-test-stage.yml`, is empty there.\n- Without it, server startup dies with `GatedRepoError: 403` on `meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B-NVFP4`. An example is [this job from #42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39348980625/job/118556303062).\n- The failure is deterministic, so reruns cannot pass it. Fail-fast then blocks the rest of stage C.\n\nScheduled `main` runs and same-repo PRs still pass, because they get the secret.\n\n## Modifications\n\nIn `TestMuseSpark12B300PD.setUpClass`, raise `unittest.SkipTest` before any setup when running in CI (`is_in_ci()`) without `HF_MUSE_SPARK_TOKEN`.\n\n- Runs that have the secret (scheduled `main` and same-repo PRs) are unchanged and keep the full coverage.\n- Local runs outside CI are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A. This is a test-only change, with no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). `pre-commit run --all-files` passed.\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). Not added: this is a CI gating change in an existing test.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not applicable.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). Not applicable.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\nValidation: there was no B300 machine for a real run. I ran the module under `unittest` with the `sglang` imports stubbed:\n\n| Case | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| CI without the token | proceeds to server setup (the 403 path) | `OK (skipped=1)`, no setup |\n| CI with the token | proceeds to setup | proceeds to setup (unchanged) |\n| Local run without the token | proceeds to setup | proceeds to setup (unchanged) |\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39428811662](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39428811662)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39428811697](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39428811697)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39428811576](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39428811576)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
